comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-26T14:37:53.572Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check evidence: searched all statuses for exact ESLint 10.9.1, @types/node 26.3.0, TypeScript 7, npm-package-arg 14, and dependency refresh owners. No item owns the two current compatible patches; pm-do5b and pm-ksr40d remain canonical for the incompatible majors."
  "2026-08-26T15:49:45.715Z","harness:codex","Final dependency evidence: ESLint resolves to 10.9.1 and @types/node to 26.3.0; runtime Node declarations retain the >=22 floor. Registry census leaves only TypeScript 7 (typesript-eslint peer incompatibility, pm-do5b) and npm-package-arg 14 (Node engine incompatibility, pm-ksr40d), now linked as causal discoveries rather than generic related edges. Audit reports zero vulnerabilities; typecheck, ESLint, zero-clone, exact coverage, static quality, package artifact, npx, bunx, and packed consumer proof pass."
  "2026-08-26T15:49:59.988Z","harness:codex","Correction: the canonical TypeScript 7 blocker is the typescript-eslint 8.68 peer range, tracked by pm-do5b."
  "2026-08-26T17:43:08.096Z","harness:codex","Exact-head evidence remediation: linked-test metadata now makes exact coverage, package-artifact integrity, fresh npx, package-first packed dogfood, and deterministic npx/bunx verifier paths reproducible. Current executions pass: 583 files / 8,011 tests at 100/100/100/100; artifact 19,651,385 bytes / 1,533 files; npx package smoke; and 88-command package-first dogfood. Live registry bunx proof remains correctly separated as post-merge operational evidence."
